{"id":"brace-dot-slash-no-arm","kind":"match_glob_path","pattern":"{src/*.rs,lib/*.rs}","path":"src/m.rs","flags":["braces"],"expected":true,"source":"handwritten","note":"Baseline for the per-alternative leading ./ rows below (#395); the walker selects what this entry point accepts."}
{"id":"brace-dot-slash-one-arm","kind":"match_glob_path","pattern":"{./src/*.rs,lib/*.rs}","path":"src/m.rs","flags":["braces"],"expected":true,"source":"handwritten","note":"One leading ./ is ignored on every brace-expanded alternative, not only at the start of the source. The walker used to drop this alternative silently (#395)."}
{"id":"brace-dot-slash-one-arm-other","kind":"match_glob_path","pattern":"{./src/*.rs,lib/*.rs}","path":"lib/n.rs","flags":["braces"],"expected":true,"source":"handwritten","note":"The alternative without the prefix is unaffected by its sibling's ./ (#395)."}
{"id":"brace-dot-slash-every-arm","kind":"match_glob_path","pattern":"{./src/*.rs,./lib/*.rs}","path":"src/m.rs","flags":["braces"],"expected":true,"source":"handwritten","note":"Every alternative may carry the prefix. The walker used to reject this spelling as an unnormalized . component (#395)."}
{"id":"brace-dot-slash-nested-arm","kind":"match_glob_path","pattern":"{{./src,lib}/*.rs,x}","path":"src/m.rs","flags":["braces"],"expected":true,"source":"handwritten","note":"Nested groups expand first; the prefix is read on the expanded alternative (#395)."}
{"id":"brace-dot-slash-exposed-by-empty-arm","kind":"match_glob_path","pattern":"{x,}./src/*.rs","path":"src/m.rs","flags":["braces"],"expected":true,"source":"handwritten","note":"An empty alternative exposes a ./ that starts no source alternative; the expanded alternative is what counts (#395)."}
{"id":"brace-dot-slash-once-per-arm","kind":"match_glob_path","pattern":"./{./src/*.rs,lib/*.rs}","path":"src/m.rs","flags":["braces"],"expected":false,"source":"handwritten","note":"Exactly one prefix is ignored per alternative: ././src/*.rs keeps a . component, which no root-relative path has (#395)."}
{"id":"brace-dot-slash-later-component","kind":"match_glob_path","pattern":"src/{./a,b}/*.rs","path":"src/a/m.rs","flags":["braces"],"expected":false,"source":"handwritten","note":"A ./ that does not start the expanded alternative is an ordinary . component, not the conventional prefix (#395)."}
